Started name was green project - 1991 (James gosling and a small team at Sun Microsystems explore software for consumer devices)
After changed into named "OAK" - 1991 (The new language is named after an oak tree outside Gosling's office)
-> OAK is a satilite project. 
After name is changed into Star7 demo - 1992. (A handheld prototype (*7) shows oak code running on custom hardware)
After that it is renamed as Java - 1995 ("Oak" is already trademarked; java is publicly announced in May 1995)
Finally in 1996 it is named by JDK 1.0 (First official release (January -1996) -java goes mainstream).

Versions 
